<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10583" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιτείνω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τενῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					604a
				</span></i>
			 (v.l.):—<i>stretch, strain back,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τοὔπισθεν τὰ σπαπτία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					888a20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ἡνίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.13d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>stretch out</i> or <i>offer in return,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήπἰ ἀντὶ νηπίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					891
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>act</i> or <i>strive against, resist,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιβουλίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					4.37
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.161
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				547b
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παντὶ λόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					91c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					256a
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1126b15
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός</span>
			=
			<i>with respect to</i>): abs., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.219
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				714
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀντέτεινον, ἀλλ᾽ εἶκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείκει καὶ οὐκ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					727d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύο ἄνδρες ἀντιτείνοντες</span>”
				<i>pulling one against the other,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Fract.</u>
					15
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of countries
			and places, <i>lie over against,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Them.</u>
				8
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
